WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.352
The EU AI Act: structure and the general-purpose AI chapter.

2
00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:14.851
The AI Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689) entered into force on 1 August 2024.

3
00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:29.893
It sorts AI by risk: a short list of prohibited practices (Article 5); high-risk systems in listed areas such as employment, education, credit, essential services, and law enforcement, which carry the heaviest duties;

4
00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:39.816
transparency duties for systems that interact with people or generate content (Article 50); and a separate chapter for general-purpose AI models.

5
00:00:40.096 --> 00:00:45.749
The general-purpose AI (GPAI) chapter applies to providers of the models themselves.

6
00:00:46.029 --> 00:01:03.352
Under Article 53, every GPAI provider must keep technical documentation, give downstream providers enough information to understand the model’s capabilities and limits, have a policy to comply with EU copyright law, and publish a summary of the content used for training.

7
00:01:03.632 --> 00:01:20.635
Models are presumed to have systemic risk when their cumulative training compute exceeds 10 to the 25 floating-point operations (Article 51), and their providers must additionally evaluate and adversarially test them, assess and mitigate systemic risks,

8
00:01:20.915 --> 00:01:26.952
report serious incidents to the AI Office, and ensure cybersecurity (Article 55).

9
00:01:27.232 --> 00:01:35.872
Open-source models released under qualifying licenses are exempt from some of the documentation duties, but not from the systemic-risk duties.

10
00:01:36.152 --> 00:01:39.181
The European Commission’s guidance gives the timeline.

11
00:01:39.461 --> 00:01:43.813
GPAI obligations applied from 2 August 2025.

12
00:01:44.093 --> 00:01:50.088
The Commission’s enforcement powers, including fines, apply from 2 August 2026.

13
00:01:50.368 --> 00:01:58.261
Providers of models placed on the market before 2 August 2025 have until 2 August 2027.

14
00:01:58.541 --> 00:02:15.203
Alongside the law, the Commission published a voluntary General-Purpose AI Code of Practice (July 2025) with chapters on transparency, copyright, and safety and security; providers that sign it can use adherence to demonstrate compliance,

15
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:19.856
and the Commission says it will focus enforcement on monitoring that adherence.
